      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Doorstep Delivery Handover, Inventory Verification &amp; Reassembly for Bike Transport Bags And Cases</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Upon arrival at the destination warehouse, the first step is to verify that the shipment matches the original inventory sheets. The team opens the outer cartons one by one, counting each bag and case and comparing the totals to the documented numbers.</p>
<p>Any discrepancy triggers an immediate audit: missing items are logged, the shipping carrier is notified, and a corrective action form is filed. Once the count is confirmed, the cartons are placed on the staging floor in the order indicated by the packing list to streamline the next stages.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">With the inventory verified, the focus shifts to furniture reassembly.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Each bike case is inspected for damage; if a case has been compromised, it is marked for replacement.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The reassembly process follows the manufacturer’s step‑by‑step guide: first, the frame is removed from the case, then the wheels are reattached, and finally the handlebars and seat are secured.</span></li></ul>
<p>The crew uses the supplied torque wrenches to ensure all bolts meet the specified torque settings. After assembly, the bike is run on a test track to confirm proper operation. All reassembled units are then labeled with a serial number and placed in the designated storage area, ready for dispatch or sale.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
